  - modify, adapt or create derivative works from them;
  - sublicense, sell or otherwise transfer them.

Ideas are not owned. Copyright protects the particular expression of a program, not the
concepts behind it. Understanding how something here works and then writing your own
implementation is exactly what this repository is public for. Copying the files is not.


A NOTE ON FORKING
-----------------

Because this repository is public on GitHub, GitHub's Terms of Service permit other
GitHub users to view and fork it on the GitHub platform. That is a condition of hosting
a public repository and cannot be disabled while it remains public. A fork is not a
grant of the rights withheld above: it does not permit use, modification or
redistribution of this code outside GitHub, nor its inclusion in any other project.


